  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The government of Sierra Leone in April 2023 promulgated a national minimum wage (800 NLe /$30), however the benefits of the new wage have already been eroded by inflation against a rising cost of living. Tin addition, there are other challenges affecting the well being workers in Sierra Leone. The ILO continues to work with the Sierra Leone Labour Congress (SLLC) to deepen institutional capacities required for effective engagement in addressing these challenges.

The strategy of the intervention focuses on capacity building, policy advice, trainings and programme management. The ILO with other international workers organizations is facilitating policy dialogues and instituion capacity building to promote effective function of SLLC.</narrative>
  </description>
